body:
Restart required to retarget the template library: `kalide start` captures the deck's configured `templates:` value from `kalide.yaml` at startup — the RAW value exactly as written in the file (the path string as written), with an absent key recorded as "no value" — and that raw startup value is the session's comparison baseline. On every reload the pipeline compares the currently-configured raw `templates:` value against the captured startup value: if they differ, the session is restart-required (below); if they are equal, it behaves normally. The comparison is on the raw configured value, NOT on the resolved library root: two different configured values that happen to resolve to the same directory (e.g. `../shared-lib` versus an absolute path to it) still count as a change. When the values differ — a different path, or the key added or removed — kalide does NOT retarget live and does NOT fall back to a local `templates/`: it stops serving the deck and serves the standard kalide full-page error telling the user to restart `kalide start` (every served page shows that error, per never-serve-broken-deck). The server keeps running — this is a normal error page, not a crash — so the user can fix `kalide.yaml` and/or restart. Normal serving resumes only after restarting `kalide start`, or when the raw value is edited back to exactly the one captured at startup. This applies only to a change of the configured `templates:` value: edits of files anywhere under the resolved library root (library.yaml, templates, themes, media) keep live-reloading exactly as before (templates-live-reload), and every other `kalide.yaml` change (title, author, date, theme, navigation, properties) and changes to slides/ and assets/ keep live-reloading as before (live-reload).

AC:
- start with `templates: ../shared-lib`, then edit `kalide.yaml` to `templates: ../other-lib` while `kalide start` runs: the next served page is the full-page error telling the user to restart `kalide start`, and no deck is served;
- start with `templates: ../shared-lib`, then edit it to `./../shared-lib` (a different raw value that resolves to the same root): the raw value differs, so the restart-required error is shown — the comparison is on the raw configured value, not the resolved root;
- adding the `templates:` key where there was none, or removing it where it was set, yields the same restart-required full-page error (removing the key is a raw-value change, so it is the restart error — not templates-dir-required), never a silent switch to or from a local `templates/`;
- editing the value back to exactly the startup value (`../shared-lib`) resumes normal serving of the deck without restarting;
- restarting `kalide start` after the retarget serves the deck from the new root (`../other-lib`);
- with the configured value unchanged, editing a file under the resolved library root (e.g. a template layout) still live-reloads, and editing any other `kalide.yaml` key still live-reloads — the restart requirement does not apply to them;
- the error is the standard kalide full-page error and the process keeps running (the listening port stays bound); it is neither a crash nor a partially rendered deck.
